text:
To turn the mock-up into a colorful and interactive website, we can add a web page with a text input field and buttons to display and clear the joke. The joke can be replaced by using JavaScript when the user submits the input field or clears the text. Here's a simple HTML structure, and some JavaScript code to handle user interaction:

HTML:
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>My Joke Website</title>
    <style>
        input[type="text"] {
            padding: 10px;
            border: 1px solid #ccc;
            border-radius: 3px;
            width: 300px;
        }

        .joke-display {
            margin: 20px 0;
        }

        button {
            padding: 10px 20px;
            border: 1px solid #ccc;
            border-radius: 3px;
            font-size: 14px;
        }

        button[type="submit"] {
            background-color: #0F7B94;
            color: #fff;
            text-align: center;
            cursor: pointer;
        }

        button[type="clear"] {
            background-color: #ffe4d5;
            color: #0077be;
            text-align: center;
            cursor: pointer;
        }
    </style>
</head>
